issue_context.body:
### Terraform Version

```
Terraform v1.4.0-dev
on darwin_amd64
+ provider registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/tfcoremock v0.1.2
```


### Terraform Configuration Files

```terraform
resource "tfcoremock_dynamic_resource" "example" {
  nested_map = {
    "foo" = {
      boop = true
      beep = "foop"
    }
    "bar" = {
      beep = "barp"
    }
  }
}
```

`dynamic_resources.json`:
```json
{
  "tfcoremock_dynamic_resource": {
    "attributes": {
      "nested_map": {
        "type": "map",
        "required": true,
        "map": {
          "type": "object",
          "object": {
            "boop": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "optional": true
            },
            "beep": {
              "type": "string",
              "optional": true
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Debug Output

N/A

### Expected Behavior

```shellsession
$ terraform show
# tfcoremock_dynamic_resource.example:
resource "tfcoremock_dynamic_resource" "example" {
    id         = "77a6363a-c9eb-1b65-7e75-646ec3591b7b"
    nested_map = {
        "foo" = {
            boop = true
            beep = "foop"
        }
        "bar" = {
            beep = "barp"
        }
    }
}
```

### Actual Behavior

```shellsession
$ terraform show
# tfcoremock_dynamic_resource.example:
resource "tfcoremock_dynamic_resource" "example" {
    id         = "77a6363a-c9eb-1b65-7e75-646ec3591b7b"
    nested_map = {
        # (2 unchanged elements hidden)
    }
}
```

### Steps to Reproduce

1. `terraform init`
2. `terraform apply -auto-approve`
3. `terraform show`

### Additional Context

`terraform show` (when showing state, not a plan) should not use the concise diff rendering format, as it will never be displaying a change where we want to omit unchanged values.

### References

Noted as part of #32619 (thanks, @bendbennett!)
